x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 and D2 variants of an *implicit* constructor and destructor on this target, and cxx1 emits C1/D1 beside them - so cxx1 has _ZN1DC1Ev, _ZN1DD1Ev and _ZN2cc4BaseC1Ev where clang has none of the three. A compiler-written special member is inline by nature and has no out-of-line form to move to, which is why this case cannot dodge it the way its written members do. The two are identical for a class with no virtual bases and both are mergeable definitions, so the extra symbol costs object size and nothing else. implicit-move.nonames and move-constructor.nonames record the same fact. Darwin and Windows agree on every name.
